# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run on quantum hardware with IBM Quantum Compute Service {#run-on-quantum-hardware-with-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "Jalankan di hardware kuantum dengan IBM Quantum Compute Service {#run-on-quantum-hardware-with-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service, formerly called the Qiskit Runtime Service, is the cloud-based service for executing quantum computations on IBM Quantum hardware. The `qiskit-ibm-runtime` package is a client for that service, and is the successor to the Qiskit IBM Provider.  Quantum Compute streamlines quantum computations and provides optimal implementations of the Qiskit primitive base classes for IBM Quantum hardware. To get started with IBM Quantum primitives, visit the [documentation](/guides/primitives).\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service, dulu bernama Qiskit Runtime Service, adalah layanan berbasis cloud untuk menjalankan komputasi kuantum di hardware IBM Quantum. Paket `qiskit-ibm-runtime` adalah client untuk layanan itu, dan merupakan penerus Qiskit IBM Provider.  Quantum Compute menyederhanakan komputasi kuantum dan menyediakan implementasi optimal dari base class primitive Qiskit untuk hardware IBM Quantum. Untuk mulai memakai primitive IBM Quantum, kunjungi [dokumentasi](/guides/primitives).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute is designed to use additional classical and quantum compute resources, including techniques such as error suppression and error mitigation, to return a higher-quality result from executing quantum circuits on quantum processors. Examples include dynamical decoupling for error suppression, and readout mitigation and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) for error mitigation. Learn how to configure these options on the [Configure error mitigation](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) page.\n"
msgstr "Quantum Compute dirancang untuk memakai sumber daya komputasi klasik dan kuantum tambahan, termasuk teknik seperti penekanan error dan mitigasi error, untuk menghasilkan hasil berkualitas lebih tinggi dari eksekusi circuit kuantum di prosesor kuantum. Contohnya dynamical decoupling untuk penekanan error, serta readout mitigation dan zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) untuk mitigasi error. Pelajari cara mengonfigurasi opsi ini di halaman [Konfigurasi mitigasi error](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute also includes three types of execution modes for running your quantum program on IBM&reg; hardware: [Job, Session, and Batch](/guides/execution-modes), each of which have different use cases and implications for the quantum job queue. A Job is a single query to a primitive that can be run over a specified number of shots. Sessions allow you to efficiently run multiple jobs in iterative workloads on quantum computers. Batch mode allows you to submit all your jobs at once for parallel processing. Note that Open Plan users cannot submit session jobs.\n"
msgstr "Quantum Compute juga mencakup tiga jenis execution mode untuk menjalankan program kuantum kamu di hardware IBM&reg;: [Job, Session, dan Batch](/guides/execution-modes), yang masing-masing punya kasus penggunaan dan implikasi berbeda terhadap antrean job kuantum. Job adalah satu query ke primitive yang bisa dijalankan dengan jumlah shot tertentu. Session memungkinkan kamu menjalankan banyak job secara efisien dalam workload iteratif di komputer kuantum. Batch mode memungkinkan kamu mengirim semua job sekaligus untuk diproses secara paralel. Perlu diingat bahwa pengguna Open Plan tidak bisa mengirim session job.\n"

